{{also|Cognac}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|cognac}}, from {{m|en|Cognac}}, a city in France, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|Comniacum}}, from the name {{m|es|Cominius}} + Gallo-Roman suffix [[-acum]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɒn.jæk/|/ˈkoʊn.jæk/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|konjac|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Cognac (drink)}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[brandy]] [[distilled]] from [[white wine]] in the [[region]] around [[Cognac]] in [[France]].
#: ''Major manufacturers add a small proportion of caramel to colour their '''cognacs'''.''

